The recent debate about human population leads me to suspect that some may
like my modest proposal for a population "control" policy that will achieve
the goal of a much more libertarian world.

It consists of high fertility and child exposure.  The point is to bring as
many people as possible into existence that will never have any experience
of being depedent upon any parental figure, and thus will never learn how
nice such depedency can be, and thus will never try to get the State to
become a surrogate parent.

By strictly libertarian methods, the way to do this would be to pay people
to expose their children as well as to have them in the first place.  A
less libertarian method would be coercive policies to do things like ban
contraception and abortion as well as any kind of child-support at all.
Needless to say, I think the former would be preferable.

Of course, since child exposure is prohibited most places, it would have to
be legalized.

