Objection: irrelevant.  Rights != right and wrong.  Rights = permissible
and impermissible.  What would be relevant is if hunters thought that it
were impermissible for some things to be done to their prey.

>Animal rights are no sillier a concept than human rights.

Bullshit.  Rights are based upon reason.  Beasts have no reason, therefore
there's no reason for them to have rights.  Disagreement about this always
stems from misunderstanding of rights or reason.  Some argue that rights
are based upon something else, others that beasts have reason.  Both are
false.

Of course, few posters ever let their misunderstanding of the issues at
hand or the falsehood of their claims slow down their typing, so I don't
expect the signal/noise ratio to increase much, and have excluded this
thread.

